    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "Colour blend and rectangle hit test with tuple-based struct values.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "STRUCT-LIKE VALUES\n\nA struct bundles several fields into one value. The standard library models its small structs as\ntuples with a Make node (fields in -> one value out) and a Break node (one value -> fields out):\n  Color (r, g, b, a)    Rect (position, size)    Transform (position, rotation, scale)\nPass the whole bundle down one wire instead of four. Here: blend two colours and compare the result\nwith the colour we expect, and test a point against a rectangle.\nClass variables hold single values (numbers, text, booleans), so the collection itself lives on the wires between nodes and only the answers are stored in variables.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          250.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "COLOUR\nMake Color builds (1.0, 0.25, 0.0, 1.0) and blue. Color Lerp blends halfway (t = 0.5) to (0.5, 0.125, 0.5, 1.0); Color Eq Approx confirms it matches, within a tolerance.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          440.0
        ],
        "size": [
          960.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "tint",
          "blue",
          "mix",
          "want",
          "same"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "RECTANGLE\nMake Rect takes a position vector and a size vector: ((10, 10), (20, 20)). Rect Contains asks whether the point (15, 15) lies inside: true.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          1120.0
        ],
        "size": [
          960.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
